                { "text": "。", "reading": null }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "notes": "This pattern works with any noun: 料理を勉強しています (studying cooking), 音楽を勉強しています (studying music)."
        },
        {
          "id": "theme-si-hajimemashite",
          "title": "はじめまして・よろしくおねがいします",
          "explanation": "はじめまして (hajimemashite) is the standard first-meeting greeting, equivalent to 'Nice to meet you'. よろしくおねがいします (yoroshiku onegai shimasu) literally means 'I humbly ask for your good favour' — always said at the end of a self-introduction.",
          "structure": "はじめまして。[自己紹介] よろしくおねがいします。",
          "examples": [
            {
              "japanese": "はじめまして。よろしくおねがいします。",
